# postui — caps.decl
#
# Wave: postui v1 (Ratatui-parity TUI widget library)
# Milestone: M1 (skeleton + cell buffer + minimal Block widget)
# Doc: docs/design.md §2.1 (KIND_TUI_CANVAS cap model), §2.5 (input
#      handling), §4 (cross-repo dependency chain).
#
# postui is the TUI widget library that lets ring-3 tools build rich
# multi-pane interactive screens. Its cap footprint is deliberately
# minimal: postui itself holds authority over the terminal-rendering
# capabilities its callers already have; it never mints, brokers, or
# owns caps on the caller's behalf beyond what a draw + present cycle
# requires. Every entry below is what a consumer must confer on a
# postui-linked binary at exec time (via the InitCap sidecar or an
# equivalent seeding path); postui does not upgrade any authority
# beyond the request set.
#
# Every KIND below is named symbolically because the wave-89
# KIND_TUI_CANVAS kernel landing (paideia-os R89.M1-001..003, docs/
# design.md §4) is a hard prerequisite of postui.M1-004 and later.
# libpdx-cap's caps.decl parser is textual and accepts the symbolic
# name until the numeric ordinal is pinned here at M1-004 landing time
# (design.md §2.1 already commits the ordinal to 0x1A6).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# KIND_TUI_CANVAS — the render substrate (docs/design.md §2.1)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The one KIND that is uniquely postui's. Every consumer that draws a
# frame holds one canvas cap per rendering surface (typically one per
# process for a fullscreen TUI; multiple for a compositor-style app
# splitting into per-region sub-canvases at M4+).
#
# Rights layout (mirrors R_TTY_* discipline; see docs/design.md §2.1
# "Rights" table):
#
#   R_TUI_PRESENT   0x002   diff + emit a frame (the write analogue)
#   R_TUI_INVOKE    0x008   query ops (rows, cols, id, tty_id)
#   R_TUI_RESIZE    0x010   TUI_OP_RESIZE / TUI_OP_CLEAR
#   R_TUI_REVOKE    0x020   teardown the row
#   R_TUI_MINT      0x200   derive a narrower child (reserved; no v1 caller)
#   R_TUI_OBSERVE   0x400   debug printer
#
# postui M1's rendering path exercises PRESENT (per-frame) + INVOKE
# (rows/cols query at Terminal::init) + RESIZE (on SIGWINCH-equivalent
# TTY resize event) + REVOKE (Terminal::teardown). MINT is reserved
# for a later multi-canvas compositor (out of v1 scope, §2.1 note).
# OBSERVE is opt-in for debug-tap consumers only.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# KIND_TTY — the input + physical-sink substrate (docs/design.md §2.5)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Two independent uses:
#
#   * write — a canvas is provably wired to a live KIND_TTY at mint
#     time (docs/design.md §2.1: the row's tty_slot is validated via
#     tty_tail_valid at cap_handler_tui_canvas mint). TUI_OP_PRESENT
#     emits its ANSI byte stream through the tty_slot, so the write
#     right is transitively required even though postui code never
#     issues TTY_OP_WRITE itself -- the caller's exec-time InitCap
#     seeding must carry it so the mint gate does not refuse.
#
#   * read — the primary input path (docs/design.md §2.5). Once
#     paideia-os #1986 (R66v2.POS-001, KIND_TTY raw-mode +
#     TTY_OP_READ) lands, postui M1-005's Terminal::init probes it
#     via TTY_OP_SET_RAW; if the cap lacks R_TTY_READ or the op is
#     refused, postui falls back to sys_read(0) against the VFS fd.
#     The fallback is explicitly temporary (design.md §2.5, M4-007
#     tracks its removal); the caps.decl declares read up front so
#     downstream tooling sees the eventual runtime dependency at M1.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# KIND_MEMORY — the canvas backing store (docs/design.md §2.1)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# KIND_TUI_CANVAS derives over KIND_MEMORY (= KIND_PAGE, 4), following
# the kind_gpu_bo / kind_display_plane precedent. The caller mints a
# KIND_MEMORY region sized 2 * rows * cols * CELL_BYTES (§2.1 backing
# buffer layout) and hands it to sys_cap_derive(KIND_TUI_CANVAS, ...)
# at Terminal::init. The KIND_MEMORY authority is not held by postui
# beyond the derive call -- the derived canvas cap is what postui
# subsequently invokes for every PRESENT.
requires:
- KIND_TUI_CANVAS(present, invoke, resize, revoke)
- KIND_TTY(write, read)
- KIND_MEMORY(mint, revoke)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Declared output schemas
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# postui is a library, not a service -- it does not itself bind an
# app_pipe_fd. Every widget's draw() emits a per-widget
# {WidgetName}View@0.1 schema (docs/design.md §2.3 semantic-pipe
# integration; §2.6 widget catalog) THROUGH a KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT the
# CONSUMER binds at startup. The schemas below are the surface
# postui promises to emit once the widget bodies land (M1-006 Block,
# M2-004..M2-008, M3-002..M3-006, M4-*); at M1-001 the emitter path
# is scaffolding only. Consumers declare the endpoint (see e.g.
# postui-top's own caps.decl at postui-top.M1); postui declares the
# schema names it will produce, per the libpdx-semantic-pipe
# 32-byte-BLAKE3 schema-hash contract.
#
# Every schema is frozen at @0.1 for postui v1; libpdx-semantic-pipe's
# 4-rule version-tolerance matrix (v1.0.0, already shipped) governs
# what a subsequent @0.2 may change without breaking an old
# subscriber (design.md §2.3 explicitly reuses this rather than
# reinvents versioning).
declares_output_schemas:
- BlockView@0.1
- ParagraphView@0.1
- ListView@0.1
- TableView@0.1
- TabsView@0.1
- GaugeView@0.1
- SparklineView@0.1
- BarChartView@0.1
- ChartView@0.1
- CanvasView@0.1
- TreeView@0.1
- CalendarView@0.1
- ScrollbarView@0.1
- TextInputView@0.1
